add(3,'unproved claim',[146],['13','31–37'],'b=b_1b_2','For locally split χ-trivialised extensions, the chosen product parameter is b_1b_2. If the coordinate-change scalar is χ, replacing b_i by b_i+χu_i changes the product by χ(u_1b_2+b_1u_2+χu_1u_2).','The ring-valued coordinate model assumes trivial rank-one endpoints; the Hom-valued formulation uses tensor products. The χ reading is conditional, not an alteration.','The circled product and both change-of-splitting formulas are present, but neither coherence nor a global inverse is asserted here.')
add(4,'unpursued implication',[146],['5–9'],'\\begin{pmatrix}2&0\\\\-b_1&0\\end{pmatrix}','The displayed matrices P=[[2,0],[-b,0]] and Q=[[0,0],[b,2]] satisfy P+Q=2I, PQ=QP=0, P²=2P and Q²=2Q over every commutative ring.','These four identities are a reconstruction of what the displayed entries imply; half-projectors require 2 to be invertible.','The matrices are on the page; the integral identities are the earlier run’s correctly delimited calculation, not a separately stated authorial theorem.')
