add(39,'idea of the earlier run',[166,168,170],['1183–1192','1263–1278','1298–1331'],'une application can. d’extensions','Under the explicit endpoint signs in the written pushout/pullback diagrams, χ=0 with L_i=M_i=O_X, π_i=ψ_i and ϖ_i=−α_i produces opposite extension classes. On a characteristic-zero elliptic curve, choosing nonzero e and the other split gives e versus −e, so no strict endpoint-fixing comparison exists.','This is the earlier run’s conditional counterexample, not Grothendieck’s claim. A sign-twisted comparison is possible; verification is recorded separately.','The note carefully restricts what it refutes; the source diagrams permit the stipulated test, with the uncertain equality branch retained.')
