add(41,'unproved claim',[172,192],['1353–1364','2331–2335'],'u=2u_1u_2+b_2u_1+b_1u_2','For a commutative ring R and A_i=R[u_i]/(u_i²+b_i u_i+c_i), the tensor element v=2u_1u_2+b_2u_1+b_1u_2 satisfies v²+b_1b_2v+b_1²c_2+b_2²c_1−4c_1c_2=0.','The displayed local equation is made precise by the monic free presentations; no injection into the tensor product is assumed.','Both the product element and its coefficients are written. Universal recomputation is attached separately.')
add(42,'unpursued implication',[172],['1360–1363'],'δ=b²−4c=δ_1δ_2','With b=b_1b_2 and c=b_1²c_2+b_2²c_1−4c_1c_2, b²−4c=(b_1²−4c_1)(b_2²−4c_2). Consequently the product is finite étale precisely when both input quadratic algebras are finite étale.','The étale consequence uses the standard discriminant criterion for finite locally free quadratic algebras; it is not separately stated on172.','The identity is explicitly displayed. The note does not confuse vanishing discriminant with a classification of inseparable or nonreduced algebras.')
add([43,76],'unproved claim',[172,192],['1367–1368','2335–2339'],'injectif sauf si car.2 et b_1=b_2=0; ça croule','Over a field the tensor-generator map from the abstract rank-two algebra fails to be injective exactly in characteristic2 with b_1=b_2=0. Over a general ring the criterion instead involves the common annihilator of 2,b_1,b_2.','The field restriction is the strongest unconditional modern reading of the terse exception; a universal-ring exception would be too strong.','The two leaves describe the same tensor-realization failure. The abstract monic algebra remains rank two; neither passage retracts its existence.','corrected')
add(44,'idea of the earlier run',[172,192],['1367–1368','2335–2339'],'A\\hookrightarrow A_1\\otimes A_2','For i(1)=1 and i(t)=2u_1u_2+b_2u_1+b_1u_2, ker(i)=Ann_R(2,b_1,b_2)·t. As an R-module map i is split injective iff (2,b_1,b_2)=R. For R=Z/4 and b_i=c_i=0,2t is a nonzero kernel element.','This exact general-ring refinement is the earlier run’s calculation, not stated by Grothendieck.','The four coefficients of i(a+dt) are (a,db_2,db_1,2d); this gives both the kernel and split criterion without additional assumptions.')
add(45,'unproved claim',[172],['1370–1398'],'f+\\bar f; ... 2','Let B=A_1⊗A_2, σ_i(u_i)=−b_i−u_i and T=I+σ_1⊗σ_2. Define q:B→A by q(1)=2,q(u_1)=−b_1,q(u_2)=−b_2,q(u_1u_2)=t+b_1b_2. Then iq=T and qi=2I_A, so T²=2T.','The explicit q matrix reconstructs the drawn factorization; uncertain arrow labels are not identified merely by the matrix calculation.','The symmetrizer and quotient factor2 appear on the leaf. The note correctly avoids calling T an idempotent when2 is not invertible.')
